## 6. Household duplicate detection & shared-household-id logic (compares addresses)

**`RejectDuplicateHousehold.java`** — duplicate detection comparing last name + address:
```java
public class RejectDuplicateHousehold {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
            throws DuplicateHouseholdException {
        if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) {
            return;
        }
        String lastName = normalize(request.getLastName());
        String address = normalize(request.getAddress());
        for (Owner owner : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (lastName.equals(normalize(owner.getLastName()))
                    && address.equals(normalize(owner.getAddress()))) {
                throw new DuplicateHouseholdException(request.getLastName(), request.getAddress());
            }
        }
    }
    private static String normalize(String value) {
        return value == null ? "" : value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase();
    }
}
```

**`AssignHousehold.java`** — shared `householdId` assignment comparing last name + address:
```java
public class AssignHousehold {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, @Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        if (!Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) {
            return;
        }
        String lastName = normalize(owner.getLastName());
        String address = normalize(owner.getAddress());
        String householdId = String.format("HH-%08X", (lastName + "|" + address).hashCode());
        owner.setHouseholdId(householdId);
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (lastName.equals(normalize(existing.getLastName()))
                    && address.equals(normalize(existing.getAddress()))) {
                existing.setHouseholdId(householdId);
                ownerRepository.save(existing);
            }
        }
    }
    private static String normalize(String value) {
        return value == null ? "" : value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase();
    }
}
```

Both have their **own private `normalize()`** (trim + collapse whitespace + lowercase) — duplicated logic. This is a prime candidate for extraction/reuse if you build a shared address normalizer. Note both these run **before** `BuildOwner`; `RejectDuplicateHousehold` uses `request.getAddress()`, while `AssignHousehold` uses `owner.getAddress()` (post-build). If you normalize the DTO address early in the chain, both comparisons would then operate on already-normalized values.

**`DuplicateHouseholdException.java`** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateHouseholdException.java`, message `"Household already in use: <lastName>, <address>"`, handled → 409 via `.../escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateHouseholdException.yml`.

