## 8. Existing normalization utilities

There is **no address normalization utility**. Existing normalization assets you can model on / reuse:

- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/E164.java`** — a standalone stateless util class (`public static String toE164(String)`), the closest template for a new `AddressNormalizer`/`Address` util:
```java
public final class E164 {
    private E164() {}
    public static String toE164(String raw) {
        if (raw == null) return null;
        boolean explicit = raw.trim().startsWith("+");
        String digits = raw.replaceAll("\\D", "");
        if (!explicit) {
            if (digits.startsWith("0")) digits = digits.substring(1);
            digits = "61" + digits;
        }
        if (digits.length() < 8 || digits.length() > 15) return null;
        return "+" + digits;
    }
}
```
- `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` / `NormalizeOwnerEmail` (function-class pattern, mutate `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` in place) — shown in §2.
- The private `normalize()` methods duplicated in `RejectDuplicateHousehold` and `AssignHousehold` (trim + collapse whitespace + lowercase) — §6.

